{
  "findings": [
    {
      "cwe_id": "CWE-862",
      "explanation": "The PR removes the @require_role(\"admin\") decorator from the /admin/audit endpoint (app/routes/admin.py:32-33). The blueprint is registered with no blueprint-level or app-level auth (app/__init__.py:23 registers admin_bp under /admin with no before_request hook; grep confirms no before_request exists in the app). The sibling /admin/stats endpoint (lines 18-19) retains @require_role(\"admin\"), confirming the per-endpoint decorator is the only guard. With the decorator removed, GET /admin/audit returns audit log entries (user_id, action) to any unauthenticated request, violating the policy that every /admin endpoint requires the admin role.",
      "evidence": [
        {"type": "code", "file": "app/routes/admin.py", "lines": [32, 33], "content": "@admin_bp.route(\"/audit\", methods=[\"GET\"])\ndef audit_log():"},
        {"type": "code", "file": "app/routes/admin.py", "lines": [18, 19], "content": "@admin_bp.route(\"/stats\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n@require_role(\"admin\")"},
        {"type": "code", "file": "app/__init__.py", "lines": [23, 23], "content": "app.register_blueprint(admin_bp, url_prefix=\"/admin\")"},
        {"type": "policy", "source": "security-policy.md", "content": "## 4. Admin panel\n- Every endpoint under `/admin` requires the **admin** role, enforced with `@require_role(\"admin\")`.\n- There are NO alternative access paths to admin functionality: no debug headers, no secret query parameters, no IP allowlists."},
        {"type": "policy", "source": "api-spec.md", "content": "| `/admin/audit` | GET | admin only |"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the @require_role(\"admin\") decorator on the audit_log route so the endpoint enforces the admin role as required by policy §4 and the API spec.",
      "file": "app/routes/admin.py",
      "line": 32
    }
  ]
}

The section under review is an authorization change (removal of `@require_role("admin")`), not a SQL-injection change. The `audit_log` query uses a fixed SQLAlchemy ORM query with no attacker-influenced values, so there is no CWE-89 candidate in this section.

